hadiths[10]{hadithnumber,text}:
"959","993 - Ibn al-Muqri and Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, say: By my father! The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah forbids you swearing by your fathers. He said: By Allah, I never swore by him after that, neither deliberately nor quoting. The hadith is that of Ibn al-Muqri."
"960","994 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Hisham informed me, from al-Hasan, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Samura, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not swear by your fathers, nor by the taghuts."
"961","995 - Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Khasib and Abdullah ibn Hashim narrated to us, they said: Waki' narrated to us, from Ali ibn al-Mubarak, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Qilabah, from Thabit ibn al-Dahhak, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever swears falsely by a religion other than Islam is as he said. And he was among those who pledged allegiance under the tree."
"962","996 - Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: Isa informed us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, regarding the word of Allah Almighty: Allah does not hold you accountable for idle talk in your oaths: she said: It was revealed concerning a man saying: Yes, by Allah, and No, by Allah."
"963","997 - Abu Sa'id al-Ashajj narrated to us, he said: Waki' narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever swears a binding oath by which he seizes the wealth of a Muslim man, lying therein, will meet Allah, mighty and majestic, while He is angry with him. Then there came down: Those who purchase with the covenant of Allah and their oaths a small price. Then al-Ash'ath ibn Qays entered and said: What is Abu Abd al-Rahman narrating to you? We said: Such and such. He said: He spoke the truth; it was revealed concerning me. There was a dispute between me and a man of my people over some land of ours, so I brought him before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Your proof. And I had no proof, so he said to him: Swear. I said: O Messenger of Allah, then he will swear. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever swears a binding oath by which he seizes the wealth of a Muslim man, lying therein, will meet Allah, mighty and majestic, while He is angry with him. Then there came down: Those who purchase with the covenant of Allah and their oaths a small price, the verse."
"964","998 - Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abu Usamah narrated to us, he said: Hashim ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Nistas informed me, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with them both, say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No man swears a sinful oath at this pulpit of mine, even over a green tooth-stick, except that he takes his seat in the Fire."
"965","999 - Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever swears an oath then says: If Allah wills, has made an exception."
"966","1000 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Ibn Awn informed us, from al-Hasan, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you swear an oath and then see something better than it, do what is better and expiate your oath."
"967","1001 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar informed us, from Hammam ibn Munabbih, who said: I heard Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, say: Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If one of you persists in his oath concerning his family, it is more sinful for him before Allah than the expiation He commanded."
"968","1002 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from a man of the Ansar, that he came with a black slave-girl and said: O Messenger of Allah, I owe a believing slave, so if you consider this one a believer I shall free her. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you testify that there is no god but Allah? She said: Yes. He said: Do you testify that I am the Messenger of Allah? She said: Yes. He said: Do you believe in resurrection after death? She said: Yes. He said: Then free her."
